  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vishwa Enterprise, Through Its ... vs Union Of India, Through Its Secretary, ... on 8 April, 2021 Author: Prathiba M. Singh Bench: Prathiba M. Singh Digitally Signed By:DINESH Singh Nayal Signing Date:09.04.2021 18: $~8 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + W.P.(C) 8752/2020 Vishwa Enterprise, Through Its Proprietor Sh. Mohit Bhasin ..... Petitioner Through: Mr. Akhil Krishan Maggu, Advocate. versus Union Of India, Through Its Secretary, Government Of India, Department Of Revenue, Ministry Of Finance & Ors. ..... Respondents Through: Mr. Ajay Digpaul, Cgsc with Mr. Abhishek Khanna, Gp & Mr Kamal R. Digpaul, Advocate for Uoi. Mr. Ruchir Mishra & Mr. Mukesh Tiwari, Advocates (M-9811673689) Mr. Rakesh Chaudhary, Advocate for R-4. Coram: Justice Prathiba M. Singh Order",
    "facts": "This hearing has been done through hybrid mode (physical and virtual hearing). 2. The present petition relates to a consignment of Areca nuts which have been seized by the Customs authorities under Section 110 of the Customs Act, 1962, on the ground that they are not fit for human consumption. The Custom authorities have relied upon the test reports of Respondent No. 4 - Food Safety Standards Authority of India (hereinafter 'FSSAI') to hold back the said goods. Since the Petitioner is incurring a huge cost for retaining the goods at the Customs authorities, the prayer of the Digitally Signed By:DINESH SINGH NAYAL Signing Date:09.04.2021 18:13:10 Petitioner is that the Petitioner may be permitted to re-export these goods to the supplier itself. 3. Mr. Harpreet Singh, ld. Counsel submits that re-export would be permissible in accordance with Vishwa Enterprise, Through Its ... vs Union Of India, Through Its Secretary, ... on 8 April, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/81282387/ 1 Section 51 of the Customs Act, 1962 and if the Petitioner applies for re-exportation/exportation of the products, the same would be considered and processed in accordance with law.",
